[
  {
    "context": "Workspace",
    /*
      🐧 linux: adapted from the macOS repo, which builds everything on a "superkey"
      (ctrl-alt-cmd-shift, remapped onto capslock) plus ctrl-alt-cmd for chords that
      would otherwise collide with Raycast. Neither survives here: `cmd` does not
      exist on Linux, so those bindings simply never fire.

      Most of them turned out to be unnecessary rather than in need of translation.
      Zed's own Linux defaults already provide both halves, distinguished by whether
      ctrl is held on the second key of the chord:

        ctrl-k ctrl-<arrow>   workspace::ActivatePane<Dir>   (was ctrl-alt-cmd-<arrow>)
        ctrl-k <arrow>        pane::Split<Dir>               (was cmd-k cmd-<arrow>)

      So only the two with no Linux equivalent are bound here.

      🗒️ note: the macOS splits are also lossier — cmd-k cmd-up and cmd-k cmd-down
      both fire SplitHorizontal, and left/right both fire SplitVertical, so four keys
      reach two actions. The Linux defaults give four distinct directions instead,
      which is why they are left alone rather than overridden to match.
    */
    "bindings": {
      // pane::keybinds — no Linux default; direct translation of cmd-k cmd-x.
      "ctrl-k ctrl-x": "pane::JoinAll",
      // project_panel::keybinds — was ctrl-alt-cmd-x; ctrl-alt-x is unbound on Linux.
      "ctrl-alt-x": "project_panel::CollapseAllEntries",
    },
  },
  // AI Bindings
  {
    "context": "Editor && edit_prediction && showing_completions",
    "bindings": {
      "tab": "editor::AcceptEditPrediction",
    },
  },
]
